1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,613
He studied for six months.

2
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:04,411
He paid three thousand two hundred crowns.

3
00:00:04,531 --> 00:00:08,143
And he failed the exam –
because he was one minute late.

4
00:00:08,263 --> 00:00:09,408
This is not a joke.

5
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:14,466
Under the official 2026 rules, anyone
who arrives late may not sit the exam.

6
00:00:14,586 --> 00:00:16,662
They must register and pay again.

7
00:00:16,782 --> 00:00:22,586
And after a failed exam, the next attempt is
possible three months later at the earliest.

8
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:27,127
So today we will go through
the whole journey together.

9
00:00:27,247 --> 00:00:28,201
Registration.

10
00:00:28,321 --> 00:00:28,861
Payment.

11
00:00:28,981 --> 00:00:29,852
Preparation.

12
00:00:29,972 --> 00:00:32,164
Exam day – minute by minute.

13
00:00:32,284 --> 00:00:39,429
And every part of the exam: what is in it,
what earns points and where people lose them.

14
00:00:39,549 --> 00:00:44,859
And at the end – ten mistakes that make
people fail even when their Czech is good.

15
00:00:44,979 --> 00:00:46,978
The first one will surprise you.

16
00:00:47,098 --> 00:00:54,399
The video is long, so open the chapters in the
description – each chapter has its own time.

17
00:00:54,519 --> 00:00:59,211
And after the video, practise
on the website zkouska-a2.cz.

18
00:00:59,331 --> 00:01:03,777
There are twenty practice
exams in the new format, free.

19
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:11,603
And subscribe to the channel right now so you don't forget:
every day a lesson for each exam task comes out here.

20
00:01:11,723 --> 00:01:12,226
Let's go.

21
00:01:12,346 --> 00:01:12,849
Stop one.

22
00:01:12,969 --> 00:01:14,790
Stop one – registration.

23
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:18,915
But first a question: do
you need this exam at all?

24
00:01:19,035 --> 00:01:22,947
The A2 exam is required for
a permanent residence permit.

25
00:01:23,067 --> 00:01:29,525
You can usually apply for permanent residence
after five years of continuous stay in Czechia.

26
00:01:29,645 --> 00:01:38,932
And here is an important tip from the official website: register
for the exam before you submit your permanent residence application.

27
00:01:39,052 --> 00:01:42,257
Places are limited and the wait can take weeks.

28
00:01:42,377 --> 00:01:47,176
You usually don't have to take the exam if
you are under fifteen or sixty or older.

29
00:01:47,296 --> 00:01:50,140
Or if you studied at a
Czech school or university.

30
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:52,985
Or if your health makes communication difficult.

31
00:01:53,105 --> 00:01:58,260
But this is not a complete list – check your
situation with the Ministry of the Interior.

32
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:03,920
Registration is online only, on the
official website cestina-pro-cizince.cz.

33
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:09,430
You need a valid passport – the school
will not accept any other document.

34
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:15,610
Write your details exactly as in your
passport: first name, surname, date of birth.

35
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:19,408
On exam day the mistake
can no longer be corrected.

36
00:02:19,528 --> 00:02:23,022
You must register at least
fourteen days before the exam.

37
00:02:23,142 --> 00:02:24,417
Later is not possible.

38
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:25,431
And now a trick.

39
00:02:25,551 --> 00:02:30,187
If you choose one specific school, you
will wait until it has a free place.

40
00:02:30,307 --> 00:02:35,639
If you don't choose a school, the system
gives you the first free place at any school.

41
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:40,268
And also: if you change the school
later, you go to the end of the queue.

42
00:02:40,388 --> 00:02:47,139
When a place is free, the school will e-mail
you: date, time, address and account for payment.

43
00:02:47,259 --> 00:02:51,745
Check your mail every day – and
definitely the Spam folder too.

44
00:02:51,865 --> 00:02:54,450
Many people miss exactly this e-mail.

45
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:56,684
The school sets the date and time.

46
00:02:56,804 --> 00:03:00,628
The whole exam takes one day:
the written and the oral part.

47
00:03:00,748 --> 00:03:03,976
So pause the video and do three things.

48
00:03:04,096 --> 00:03:08,870
First – check that your passport
is valid until exam day.

49
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:13,678
Second – register and write
down your registration code.

50
00:03:13,798 --> 00:03:20,718
Third – add the school's address to your
contacts so its e-mails don't go to spam.

51
00:03:20,838 --> 00:03:22,108
Stop two – payment.

52
00:03:22,228 --> 00:03:27,742
And here is the first surprise for those
who read old advice on the internet.

53
00:03:27,862 --> 00:03:31,047
The state used to give free exam vouchers.

54
00:03:31,167 --> 00:03:33,094
They are no longer issued.

55
00:03:33,214 --> 00:03:38,840
The exam costs three thousand two
hundred crowns and you pay it yourself.

56
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,752
Every further attempt costs the same.

57
00:03:41,872 --> 00:03:45,667
Where to pay, the school will tell
you in the same e-mail with the date.

58
00:03:45,787 --> 00:03:47,951
Pay exactly according to its instructions.

59
00:03:48,071 --> 00:03:53,715
If you get a variable symbol, don't forget to include
it – otherwise the school may not find your payment.

60
00:03:53,835 --> 00:03:54,990
Remember two dates.

61
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:59,082
Fourteen days before the exam
– the last day of registration.

62
00:03:59,202 --> 00:04:07,736
Eight days before the exam – the money must be in the school's
account and you must sign the application in person at the school.

63
00:04:07,856 --> 00:04:13,706
Some schools want the payment ten days in
advance – read the e-mail from your own school.

64
00:04:13,826 --> 00:04:16,725
Whoever misses this is removed from the list.

65
00:04:16,845 --> 00:04:19,592
Signing the application is not a formality.

66
00:04:19,712 --> 00:04:25,924
Take your passport and check every letter: first
name, surname, date of birth, passport number.

67
00:04:26,044 --> 00:04:31,790
These details will be on your certificate –
and in your permanent residence application.

68
00:04:31,910 --> 00:04:35,057
One wrong letter – and a
problem at the ministry.

69
00:04:35,177 --> 00:04:37,121
And what if your plans change?

70
00:04:37,241 --> 00:04:44,279
You can cancel the exam without problems no later
than fifteen days in advance – by e-mail or in person.

71
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:49,646
Later only for a serious reason, for
example illness, and with a confirmation.

72
00:04:49,766 --> 00:04:55,152
In the e-mail write your first name,
surname, date of birth and passport number.

73
00:04:55,272 --> 00:05:04,689
What to do after this chapter: set two reminders in your phone – ten
days before, "pay", and nine days before, "sign the application".

74
00:05:04,809 --> 00:05:09,102
A few days of reserve protect
you from bank delays and queues.

75
00:05:09,222 --> 00:05:11,804
Stop three – and the most important one.

76
00:05:11,924 --> 00:05:13,020
How much to study?

77
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:15,858
The official answer: at least fifty hours.

78
00:05:15,978 --> 00:05:18,290
That is six weeks of one hour a day.

79
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,755
Here is the plan.

80
00:05:19,875 --> 00:05:26,993
Week one: do one full practice exam and
write down your points – that is your start.

81
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:36,644
Weeks two and three: the oral part – every day one topic
from Speaking 1 and one card from Speaking 2, out loud.

82
00:05:36,764 --> 00:05:41,814
Week four: stories in the past
tense and informal dialogues.

83
00:05:41,934 --> 00:05:47,070
Week five: writing – the form
and the e-mail, counting words.

84
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:53,705
Week six: two or three full practice
exams with a timer, like the real thing.

85
00:05:53,825 --> 00:05:55,179
Where to practise?

86
00:05:55,299 --> 00:05:57,552
On our website zkouska-a2.cz.

87
00:05:57,672 --> 00:06:02,463
There are twenty full practice
exams in the new 2026 format.

88
00:06:02,583 --> 00:06:04,919
A timer like at the real exam.

89
00:06:05,039 --> 00:06:07,456
Real Czech voices in listening.

90
00:06:07,576 --> 00:06:08,684
Point counting.

91
00:06:08,804 --> 00:06:11,794
And explanations in several languages.

92
00:06:11,914 --> 00:06:13,840
No registration and free.

93
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:20,333
The "My progress" section shows which part
is your weakest and what to practise today.

94
00:06:20,453 --> 00:06:28,638
And you can install the website on your phone as an app
– and practise on the tram or during your lunch break.

95
00:06:28,758 --> 00:06:34,110
And here on the channel, six short lessons
come out every day – one for each task.

96
00:06:34,230 --> 00:06:38,114
Plus big reviews: everything
from five lessons in one video.

97
00:06:38,234 --> 00:06:40,916
And every Wednesday a full listening test.

98
00:06:41,036 --> 00:06:43,452
Each playlist is one part of the exam.

99
00:06:43,572 --> 00:06:49,675
So you don't have to search for the lessons every
time – subscribe to the channel and click the bell.

100
00:06:49,795 --> 00:06:54,481
The new lesson then comes to you by
itself and the six-week plan fills itself.

101
00:06:54,601 --> 00:06:56,290
And the teacher's main tip.

102
00:06:56,410 --> 00:07:01,181
The oral part is worth forty points
– it is the biggest part of the exam.

103
00:07:01,301 --> 00:07:04,464
And you won't learn to
speak by reading silently.

104
00:07:04,584 --> 00:07:06,206
Say every answer out loud.

105
00:07:06,326 --> 00:07:11,029
In the shop, at work, at the doctor's
– speak Czech, even with mistakes.

106
00:07:11,149 --> 00:07:13,191
How do you know you are ready?

107
00:07:13,311 --> 00:07:21,620
A rule from the official website: if you score less than
eighty percent in reading and listening, repeat those parts.

108
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:27,312
When three practice exams in a row give
eighty percent or more – you are ready.

109
00:07:27,432 --> 00:07:28,191
Today's task.

110
00:07:28,311 --> 00:07:32,319
After this video open zkouska-a2.cz
and do one practice exam.

111
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:35,770
Write your result in the
comments under this video.

112
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:39,086
And come back in six weeks
and write the new one.

113
00:07:39,206 --> 00:07:42,063
The difference will pleasantly surprise you.

114
00:07:42,183 --> 00:07:42,670
Exam day.

115
00:07:42,790 --> 00:07:47,457
Now we'll go through it minute by
minute so that nothing surprises you.

116
00:07:47,577 --> 00:07:48,769
What to bring?

117
00:07:48,889 --> 00:07:53,640
A valid passport – the same
one you registered with.

118
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,045
And that's all.

119
00:07:55,165 --> 00:07:57,105
You get a pen on site.

120
00:07:57,225 --> 00:08:03,194
Dictionaries, books, notebooks
and any electronics are forbidden.

121
00:08:03,314 --> 00:08:08,158
Phone off, bag where they
tell you – not next to you.

122
00:08:08,278 --> 00:08:10,485
Arrive thirty minutes before the start.

123
00:08:10,605 --> 00:08:12,514
That is not advice – it is a rule.

124
00:08:12,634 --> 00:08:15,318
Whoever is late does not sit the exam that day.

125
00:08:15,438 --> 00:08:17,406
New registration – and new payment.

126
00:08:17,526 --> 00:08:20,508
Yes, that is the minute
from the start of the video.

127
00:08:20,628 --> 00:08:26,735
At registration you show your passport,
sign the list and get a card with a number.

128
00:08:26,855 --> 00:08:29,211
That number is your name all day.

129
00:08:29,331 --> 00:08:34,012
Passport and card lie on the desk
during the whole written part.

130
00:08:34,132 --> 00:08:36,782
The order is: Reading – forty minutes.

131
00:08:36,902 --> 00:08:38,969
Writing – twenty-five minutes.

132
00:08:39,089 --> 00:08:40,354
Then a short break.

133
00:08:40,474 --> 00:08:42,686
Listening – about forty minutes.

134
00:08:42,806 --> 00:08:46,476
And at the end the oral
part, up to fifteen minutes.

135
00:08:46,596 --> 00:08:50,431
During the written part
you may not leave the room.

136
00:08:50,551 --> 00:08:54,541
So the toilet – before the
start or during the break.

137
00:08:54,661 --> 00:08:57,953
And remember: the break is part of the exam.

138
00:08:58,073 --> 00:09:01,210
The phone stays off even during the break.

139
00:09:01,330 --> 00:09:03,900
You write the answers on the answer sheet.

140
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:06,270
Mark the correct answer with a cross.

141
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:11,202
If you make a mistake – fill in the
wrong box completely and put a new cross.

142
00:09:11,322 --> 00:09:16,199
In word tasks – cross out the wrong word
and write the correct one next to it.

143
00:09:16,319 --> 00:09:21,643
And above all: copy your answers to the
answer sheet, not just into the task booklet.

144
00:09:21,763 --> 00:09:23,308
The booklet is not marked.

145
00:09:23,428 --> 00:09:24,511
Now the points.

146
00:09:24,631 --> 00:09:31,326
The written part – reading, writing and
listening together – is worth seventy points.

147
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:33,570
You need at least forty-two.

148
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:38,942
The oral part is worth forty points,
you need at least twenty-four.

149
00:09:39,062 --> 00:09:41,748
That is sixty percent in each part.

150
00:09:41,868 --> 00:09:43,752
And both locks must open.

151
00:09:43,872 --> 00:09:45,162
And few people know this.

152
00:09:45,282 --> 00:09:52,212
The time of your oral exam is only announced on site: it can be
right after the written part, but also only in the afternoon.

153
00:09:52,332 --> 00:09:54,017
Take water and something to eat.

154
00:09:54,137 --> 00:09:59,557
In the oral exam room there are three people:
one asks questions, the others assess.

155
00:09:59,677 --> 00:10:03,184
You have no time to prepare
– you answer straight away.

156
00:10:03,304 --> 00:10:04,240
But you may ask!

157
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:07,537
If you don't understand,
say: Promiňte, nerozumím.

158
00:10:07,657 --> 00:10:08,856
Můžete to zopakovat?

159
00:10:08,976 --> 00:10:10,637
(Sorry, I don't understand.

160
00:10:10,757 --> 00:10:14,001
Can you repeat it?) You
don't lose points for that.

161
00:10:14,121 --> 00:10:17,728
Say it out loud with me
now: Promiňte, nerozumím.

162
00:10:17,848 --> 00:10:19,250
Můžete to zopakovat?

163
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:20,010
Once more!

164
00:10:20,130 --> 00:10:23,282
This sentence has already saved many exams.

165
00:10:23,402 --> 00:10:25,309
And now the exam itself.

166
00:10:25,429 --> 00:10:26,915
Part one – reading.

167
00:10:27,035 --> 00:10:30,801
Five tasks, twenty-five points, forty minutes.

168
00:10:30,921 --> 00:10:38,959
Task one: five pictures, for each you find
a short text – and three texts are extra.

169
00:10:39,079 --> 00:10:45,369
Task two: one letter or advert and
five multiple-choice questions.

170
00:10:45,489 --> 00:10:50,322
Task three: four adverts
– find who each one suits.

171
00:10:50,442 --> 00:10:56,051
Task four: six short texts with
a gap, you choose the word.

172
00:10:56,171 --> 00:11:02,461
Task five: a text and a table –
you fill in five words or numbers.

173
00:11:02,581 --> 00:11:05,677
Now a technique that saves you ten minutes.

174
00:11:05,797 --> 00:11:08,594
First read the question, then the text.

175
00:11:08,714 --> 00:11:13,978
The question tells you what to look
for: when – look for a date or time.

176
00:11:14,098 --> 00:11:15,474
How much – a number.

177
00:11:15,594 --> 00:11:16,670
Where – a place.

178
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:20,784
You don't read the whole
text, you look for the answer.

179
00:11:20,904 --> 00:11:28,027
Trap number one in reading: a word from the
text is also in an answer – and people pick it.

180
00:11:28,147 --> 00:11:29,857
But it is often a trap.

181
00:11:29,977 --> 00:11:32,882
Check the meaning, not the same words.

182
00:11:33,002 --> 00:11:43,069
The text says "closed for lunch until noon" and the option says
"open for lunch in the morning" – same words, different meaning.

183
00:11:43,189 --> 00:11:43,385
Time.

184
00:11:43,505 --> 00:11:47,293
Forty minutes for five tasks –
that is eight minutes for each.

185
00:11:47,413 --> 00:11:50,571
If you get stuck on a
question, mark it and move on.

186
00:11:50,691 --> 00:11:51,895
Come back at the end.

187
00:11:52,015 --> 00:11:58,893
And never leave boxes empty: you don't lose points for
a wrong answer, and there is a chance of guessing right.

188
00:11:59,013 --> 00:12:02,330
In task five you write the words yourself.

189
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:09,203
Write legibly, in block letters, and copy
exactly from the text: number, name, time.

190
00:12:09,323 --> 00:12:13,867
If the examiner can't read it
– the answer doesn't count.

191
00:12:13,987 --> 00:12:21,078
Exercise: on the website zkouska-a2.cz open any
version and do only the reading with a timer.

192
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:23,482
Questions first, then the text.

193
00:12:23,602 --> 00:12:26,351
You will see how much faster it goes.

194
00:12:26,471 --> 00:12:27,655
Part two – writing.

195
00:12:27,775 --> 00:12:30,811
Two tasks, twenty points, twenty-five minutes.

196
00:12:30,931 --> 00:12:34,243
And this is where most
points are lost needlessly.

197
00:12:34,363 --> 00:12:36,113
Task one – the form.

198
00:12:36,233 --> 00:12:38,919
Three questions, eight points.

199
00:12:39,039 --> 00:12:44,249
You answer each with a full
sentence, at least ten words.

200
00:12:44,369 --> 00:12:48,831
The word "yes" or "in the
park" is not an answer.

201
00:12:48,951 --> 00:12:49,345
Example.

202
00:12:49,465 --> 00:12:51,914
Question: When can you go to the doctor?

203
00:12:52,034 --> 00:12:53,326
Wrong: In the morning.

204
00:12:53,446 --> 00:13:02,445
Right: K lékaři můžu chodit ráno před prací nebo v pátek odpoledne (I
can go to the doctor in the morning before work or on Friday afternoon).

205
00:13:02,565 --> 00:13:03,344
See the trick?

206
00:13:03,464 --> 00:13:07,968
Repeat the words from the question –
and add a detail: when, where, why.

207
00:13:08,088 --> 00:13:10,023
Ten words then write themselves.

208
00:13:44,539 --> 00:13:47,252
And answer exactly the question.

209
00:13:47,372 --> 00:13:49,023
When – write a time.

210
00:13:49,143 --> 00:13:51,679
Why – write protože (because).

211
00:13:51,799 --> 00:13:53,095
Where – a place.

212
00:13:53,215 --> 00:13:59,292
The most common mistake: a nice
sentence, but to a different question.

213
00:13:59,412 --> 00:14:00,936
Task two – the e-mail.

214
00:14:01,056 --> 00:14:04,447
Twelve points – more than a whole reading task.

215
00:14:04,567 --> 00:14:07,660
You will see a situation and five pictures.

216
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,901
One sentence for each picture.

217
00:14:10,021 --> 00:14:12,890
And at least thirty-five words in total.

218
00:14:13,010 --> 00:14:13,860
Attention.

219
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:22,977
This is an official rule: if the e-mail has fewer
than thirty-five words, you get zero points.

220
00:14:23,097 --> 00:14:25,305
Not fewer points – zero.

221
00:14:25,425 --> 00:14:30,252
So after writing, count
the words with your finger.

222
00:14:30,372 --> 00:14:35,005
Better write forty to
forty-five, with a reserve.

223
00:14:35,125 --> 00:14:38,933
Here is a ready-made skeleton that always works.

224
00:14:39,053 --> 00:14:40,570
Greeting: Dobrý den.

225
00:14:40,690 --> 00:14:45,890
One sentence – why you are writing:
chtěl bych, or píšu, protože.

226
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:50,965
Then five sentences – one for
each picture, in the same order.

227
00:14:51,085 --> 00:14:54,403
And at the end: S pozdravem and your name.

228
00:15:39,089 --> 00:15:45,990
Write simple sentences, but correct ones: with a
capital letter at the start and a full stop at the end.

229
00:15:46,110 --> 00:15:50,648
In an e-mail to a company or office
use the formal you: máte, můžete.

230
00:15:50,768 --> 00:15:56,454
And don't write in a complicated way – every
extra word is a chance to make a mistake.

231
00:15:56,574 --> 00:16:03,597
Time plan for writing: eight minutes for the form, fifteen
for the e-mail, two minutes for checking and counting words.

232
00:16:03,717 --> 00:16:05,097
Go exactly in this order.

233
00:16:05,217 --> 00:16:13,678
On our channel there are forty forms and forty e-mails
with model answers – the playlists Writing 1 and Writing 2.

234
00:16:13,798 --> 00:16:16,990
Task: write one e-mail on the website today.

235
00:16:17,110 --> 00:16:19,776
The website counts the words for you.

236
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:22,031
Part three – listening.

237
00:16:22,151 --> 00:16:25,072
Five tasks, twenty-five points.

238
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:29,486
And good news: you hear each recording twice.

239
00:16:29,606 --> 00:16:33,669
Task one: five dialogues and choosing an answer.

240
00:16:33,789 --> 00:16:39,858
Task two: five announcements – at
the station, in a shop, on the radio.

241
00:16:39,978 --> 00:16:46,395
Task three: five monologues, for each
you choose an option – two are extra.

242
00:16:46,515 --> 00:16:50,317
Task four: five short dialogues and pictures.

243
00:16:50,437 --> 00:16:59,294
Task five: a voice message from which you write down
five pieces of information – time, address, price.

244
00:16:59,414 --> 00:17:00,998
The two-listening strategy.

245
00:17:01,118 --> 00:17:04,028
Before the recording quickly read the questions.

246
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,932
The first time just listen and mark an option.

247
00:17:07,052 --> 00:17:09,835
The second time check and put the final cross.

248
00:17:09,955 --> 00:17:14,317
Don't try to understand every word
– you need one piece of information.

249
00:17:14,437 --> 00:17:19,167
The most common trap in listening: two
numbers are heard in the recording.

250
00:17:19,287 --> 00:17:31,753
"The train usually leaves at eight fifteen, but today at eight forty." Listen for the words ale
(but), dnes (today), nakonec (in the end), změna (change) – the correct answer comes after them.

251
00:17:31,873 --> 00:17:34,609
In task five write numbers as digits, not words.

252
00:17:34,729 --> 00:17:36,989
The address as you hear it, but legibly.

253
00:17:37,109 --> 00:17:43,058
During the first listening make notes in the booklet,
during the second copy them to the answer sheet.

254
00:17:43,178 --> 00:17:45,905
Listening is trained only with your ears.

255
00:17:46,025 --> 00:17:52,850
Every Wednesday at seven in the evening a full
listening test with answers comes out on our channel.

256
00:17:52,970 --> 00:17:59,030
And ten minutes a day of Czech radio or news
also helps – in the car, on the way to work.

257
00:17:59,150 --> 00:18:04,064
Task: open the Listening playlist
and do the first test with paper.

258
00:18:04,184 --> 00:18:07,371
And for the next premiere click "Notify me".

259
00:18:07,491 --> 00:18:09,874
And the last part – the oral exam.

260
00:18:09,994 --> 00:18:15,027
Forty points: thirty-seven for four
tasks and three for pronunciation.

261
00:18:15,147 --> 00:18:18,340
Up to fifteen minutes that decide everything.

262
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:21,444
Task one – answering questions.

263
00:18:21,564 --> 00:18:22,745
Eight points.

264
00:18:22,865 --> 00:18:31,955
Two topics from everyday life – housing, work,
health, friends – and four questions on each.

265
00:18:32,075 --> 00:18:35,659
You see the topic, not the questions.

266
00:18:35,779 --> 00:18:41,165
Answer with a full sentence
and ideally add one detail.

267
00:18:41,285 --> 00:18:42,494
Where do you live?

268
00:18:42,614 --> 00:18:45,006
– "In Prague" – that's too little.

269
00:18:45,126 --> 00:18:50,398
"I live in Prague, in a small flat
with my family" – that's a full point.

270
00:18:50,518 --> 00:18:58,154
And listen to the tense in the question: they ask
"what did you do yesterday" – answer in the past tense.

271
00:18:58,274 --> 00:19:01,404
They ask "what will you do" – in the future.

272
00:20:35,023 --> 00:20:37,899
Task two – dialogues, twelve points.

273
00:20:38,019 --> 00:20:44,475
Two cards with a situation: for example
you are in a hotel or a service centre.

274
00:20:44,595 --> 00:20:48,804
Each has three prompts and
one question of your own.

275
00:20:48,924 --> 00:20:51,967
Here you ask and the examiner answers.

276
00:20:52,087 --> 00:20:52,814
Two rules.

277
00:20:52,934 --> 00:20:56,544
First: make a full question from the prompt.

278
00:20:56,664 --> 00:21:01,036
Not "Price?" but "How much
is a room for one night?".

279
00:21:01,156 --> 00:21:07,224
Second: here you are speaking to an
employee – use the formal you: Máte…?

280
00:21:07,344 --> 00:21:07,902
Můžete…?

281
00:21:08,022 --> 00:21:14,853
And prepare your own question in advance:
"How can I pay?" fits almost every card.

282
00:22:00,087 --> 00:22:05,808
Task three – a story based
on four pictures, ten points.

283
00:22:05,928 --> 00:22:10,396
There is one iron rule: only the past tense.

284
00:22:10,516 --> 00:22:14,464
And all four pictures – don't skip any.

285
00:22:14,584 --> 00:22:15,878
The story formula.

286
00:22:15,998 --> 00:22:21,221
Past tense: on šel, ona šla, oni
šli – and about yourself: šel jsem.

287
00:22:21,341 --> 00:22:28,607
And four linking words: nejdřív (first), potom
(then), najednou (suddenly), nakonec (finally).

288
00:22:28,727 --> 00:22:33,871
For each picture two or three
sentences: who, where, what happened.

289
00:22:33,991 --> 00:22:37,171
Don't describe the picture – tell a story.

290
00:23:09,325 --> 00:23:12,351
Task four – agreement, seven points.

291
00:23:12,471 --> 00:23:15,149
Now the examiner is your friend.

292
00:23:15,269 --> 00:23:18,907
So use the informal you: máš, chceš, můžeš.

293
00:23:19,027 --> 00:23:21,705
The picture shows three options.

294
00:23:21,825 --> 00:23:24,240
You suggest one, she says no.

295
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:26,600
You calmly suggest another.

296
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:28,086
No need to argue!

297
00:23:28,206 --> 00:23:32,752
The scheme from start to finish: Můžeme
chodit plavat (We can go swimming).

298
00:23:32,872 --> 00:23:33,250
She: no.

299
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:36,485
– Tak budeme jezdit na kole
(Then we'll go cycling).

300
00:23:36,605 --> 00:23:36,983
She: no.

301
00:23:37,103 --> 00:23:39,223
– Tak budeme běhat (Then we'll run).

302
00:23:39,343 --> 00:23:40,032
She: and why?

303
00:23:40,152 --> 00:23:45,320
– Protože běh je zdravý a nic nestojí (Because
running is healthy and costs nothing).

304
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:47,871
Done: suggestion, new suggestion, reason.

305
00:24:18,325 --> 00:24:24,557
And three points for pronunciation
– from the first to the last word.

306
00:24:24,677 --> 00:24:29,621
Speak slowly and clearly,
stress on the first syllable.

307
00:24:29,741 --> 00:24:34,040
Lengthen long vowels, as in "děkuju" or "dobře".

308
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:39,564
You don't need a perfect accent
– you need to be understood.

309
00:24:39,684 --> 00:24:43,232
The strongest exercise I know:
record yourself on your phone.

310
00:24:43,352 --> 00:24:46,599
Answer the questions from our
lessons – and listen back.

311
00:24:46,719 --> 00:24:51,831
You will hear right away where the answer is
short and where the past tense is missing.

312
00:24:51,951 --> 00:25:00,362
On the channel each of the four tasks has its own playlist –
forty lessons with a pause for your answer and with model answers.

313
00:25:00,482 --> 00:25:05,871
And on the website an examiner asks you
questions out loud, like at the real exam.

314
00:25:05,991 --> 00:25:13,663
Task for the week: fifteen minutes out loud every
day – one topic, one card, one story, one situation.

315
00:25:13,783 --> 00:25:17,483
That is exactly how long
the real oral exam takes.

316
00:25:17,603 --> 00:25:20,245
And here are the promised ten mistakes.

317
00:25:20,365 --> 00:25:21,449
Some cost points.

318
00:25:21,569 --> 00:25:23,290
And some – the whole exam.

319
00:25:23,410 --> 00:25:25,452
One – arriving late.

320
00:25:25,572 --> 00:25:31,183
Whoever is late does not
sit the exam and pays again.

321
00:25:31,303 --> 00:25:34,210
Arrive thirty minutes early.

322
00:25:34,330 --> 00:25:36,384
Two – a different document.

323
00:25:36,504 --> 00:25:38,155
Only a valid passport.

324
00:25:38,275 --> 00:25:41,697
Not a residence card, not a driving licence.

325
00:25:41,817 --> 00:25:45,967
Three – an e-mail shorter
than thirty-five words.

326
00:25:46,087 --> 00:25:48,669
Zero points for the whole task.

327
00:25:48,789 --> 00:25:50,063
Count the words.

328
00:25:50,183 --> 00:25:52,258
Four – a one-word answer.

329
00:25:52,378 --> 00:25:57,876
In the form at least ten words,
in conversation a full sentence.

330
00:25:57,996 --> 00:26:02,150
Five – present tense in the story.

331
00:26:02,270 --> 00:26:09,063
Task three – only the past
tense: ležela, šla, koupila.

332
00:26:09,183 --> 00:26:12,490
Six – mixing up formal and informal you.

333
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,802
Cards in task two – formal.

334
00:26:14,922 --> 00:26:17,800
The friend in task four – informal.

335
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:23,235
Seven – staying silent
when you don't understand.

336
00:26:23,355 --> 00:26:27,893
You may and must ask: Promiňte, nerozumím.

337
00:26:28,013 --> 00:26:31,919
Eight – empty answers in reading and listening.

338
00:26:32,039 --> 00:26:36,715
You don't lose points for a
mistake – answer everything.

339
00:26:36,835 --> 00:26:40,254
Nine – answers only in the task booklet.

340
00:26:40,374 --> 00:26:43,085
Only the answer sheet is marked.

341
00:26:43,205 --> 00:26:45,209
Copy everything in time.

342
00:26:45,329 --> 00:26:51,117
And ten, the most expensive: going to the exam
without ever having done it with a timer before.

343
00:26:51,237 --> 00:26:56,030
The official rules advise doing a practice
test first – and only then deciding.

344
00:26:56,150 --> 00:26:59,016
At least three full practice exams with a timer.

345
00:26:59,136 --> 00:26:59,860
The result.

346
00:26:59,980 --> 00:27:04,079
It comes by e-mail or SMS
within nine days of the exam.

347
00:27:04,199 --> 00:27:10,137
You passed – you collect the certificate at the
school, or they post it to you within thirty days.

348
00:27:10,257 --> 00:27:11,991
And it is valid without limit.

349
00:27:12,111 --> 00:27:13,104
Once and for good.

350
00:27:13,224 --> 00:27:14,333
You didn't pass?

351
00:27:14,453 --> 00:27:15,869
That is not the end.

352
00:27:15,989 --> 00:27:23,934
A new attempt – three months later at the earliest,
at most three times a year, and with a fee each time.

353
00:27:24,054 --> 00:27:27,390
You repeat the whole exam – written and oral.

354
00:27:27,510 --> 00:27:31,538
That's why it's better to
prepare once – and properly.

355
00:27:31,658 --> 00:27:36,537
Remember the man from the start of
the video who was one minute late?

356
00:27:36,657 --> 00:27:38,710
Now you know more than he did.

357
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:43,347
Registration, payment, preparation,
exam day and all four parts.

358
00:27:43,467 --> 00:27:46,604
Now three steps you can take right away.

359
00:27:46,724 --> 00:27:51,244
One – open zkouska-a2.cz and
do your first practice exam.

360
00:27:51,364 --> 00:27:54,256
The link is first in the description.

361
00:27:54,376 --> 00:28:01,338
Two – write your result and the date of your
exam in the comments – we answer everyone.

362
00:28:01,458 --> 00:28:05,571
Three – subscribe to the
channel and click the bell.

363
00:28:05,691 --> 00:28:08,054
And the first lesson is here.

364
00:28:08,174 --> 00:28:10,708
Oral part, topic one: about me.

365
00:28:10,828 --> 00:28:13,020
Ten questions, two minutes.

366
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:15,075
Click – and let's begin.

367
00:28:15,195 --> 00:28:16,959
Good luck at the exam!
